      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "text": "Passenger vessels' berth hire is set by separate notification and is not entered.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-2026-27",
            "page": 28,
            "section": "2.3.1"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The pilotage minimum (US$ 1,580.70 / Rs. 42,194) is stated for the first band; it is applied to the whole charge, which makes no difference above 30,000 GRT.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-2026-27",
            "page": 19
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Anchorage before berthing is free for ships working cargo at the port. Ships that stay at anchorage after sailing from the berth pay Rs. 0.021 per GRT per hour (minimum Rs. 43.44 per hour); the foreign rate is printed as 'USD 0.00075 cents' (minimum USD 1.52 per hour), which is unclear, so anchorage is not priced.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-2026-27",
            "page": 35,
            "section": "2.5.2"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Ships at the single point mooring (SPM) have their own pilotage rate (US$ 0.3107 / Rs. 11.84 per GRT); SPM calls are not priced.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-2026-27",
            "page": 37
          }
        }
